  "title": "Four-point maps on larger knot spaces, and a reason",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Proved: the self-dual maps of four held points that use all four form exactly four classes (the weighted majority, maj(a,b,a+c+d), the parity-majority switch, a+NAE(b,c,d)), only the last two can give a mod-3 bit, and general signed not-all-equal systems realise all four, so their absence is not forced by self-duality or by the law alone. Exact census, frozen, positive control passed, refereed by fresh code on 46 spaces: on 453 random knot spaces of 16, 18 and 20 points (genus 2 to 4), 179,559,422 free four-point sets give 4,303 weighted majorities, 33 maj(a,b,a+c+d), no switch and no a+NAE; four-point readings get rarer past 16 points. Proof that the switch and a+NAE never occur: not found.",
